## Lore

The hawrk-duhk, or duck-bill D-bees, are flightless, duck-billed humanoids that look like large birds with big webbed feet and large eyes. They come from the same world as their predatory cousins the hawrk-ka, who hunt them. They are a passive, group-oriented people who fight only in self defense, but they are curious and love domestic pursuits, play and exploration. Their docile nature makes them easy to capture and obedient slaves, and the Splugorth use them mostly as laborers and servants.

A male mates for life with one female. The duck-bills gather in flock-tribes that can number in the thousands, and they work together well, always trying to cooperate and help one another. They mate once a year; a female lays 2D4 eggs that hatch in four months, and the young stay with the adults for at least a year though they mature in six months. Many stay with the flock for life. Like all hawrks they are completely impervious to magic.

Alignment: any, but generally anarchist or unprincipled. Weight 300 lbs (135 kg); typically 6 to 8 ft (1.8 to 2.4 m) tall. Typical NPCs are level 1D4. Average life span fifty years. They feed on insects, amphibians, fish, crustaceans, mussels, kelp and sea plants.

## GM Notes

Slave market value 150,000 to 250,000 credits. Sold in Atlantis and occasionally found in North America, Europe and Africa. Enemies: the hawrk-ka, large predators and humanoids. Friendly to most other races.
